# Help: The core networking options the base leaves out
#
# What net/core/ and the small directories beside it build only on
# request: the classid and priority cgroups, BPF programs as route
# actions and BPF stream parsers, the packet generator, the drop
# monitor, netconsole's netpoll, ethtool's netlink interface, PHY
# timestamping, the PHY selftests
# drivers run through ethtool, Data Center Bridging, L3 master devices,
# NetLabel, NSH, PSP, kernel TLS with its offload, XDP sockets, the
# DNS resolver, the socket monitoring of netlink and packet sockets,
# networking's debug checks and fault injection, and its KUnit tests.
# NET_DEVLINK and NET_SHAPER have no prompt; netdevsim, the simulated
# device the networking selftests drive, selects them here.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - CGROUPS for the cgroups, LWTUNNEL for BPF route actions, and
#   BPF_SYSCALL with CGROUP_BPF for the BPF parts.
# - PHYLIB, which NET_SELFTESTS follows, SECURITY for NETLABEL, KEYS for
#   DNS_RESOLVER and FAULT_INJECTION_DEBUG_FS for FAIL_SKB_REALLOC.
# - DEBUG_FS for netdevsim, FTRACE with FTRACE_SYSCALLS, which selects
#   the tracepoints the drop monitor needs, and KUNIT for the tests.
# - OF, the device tree helpers net/core/of_net.c gives drivers.
#
# The tristates are tests and tools loaded on demand; no builtin/
# counterpart needed.
# See: net/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/networking/index.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_CGROUPS=y
CONFIG_LWTUNNEL=y
CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y
CONFIG_CGROUP_BPF=y
CONFIG_PHYLIB=m
CONFIG_SECURITY=y
CONFIG_KEYS=y
CONFIG_FAULT_INJECTION=y
CONFIG_FAULT_INJECTION_DEBUG_FS=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
CONFIG_FTRACE=y
CONFIG_FTRACE_SYSCALLS=y
CONFIG_KUNIT=y
CONFIG_OF=y

#
# net/core
#
CONFIG_CGROUP_NET_CLASSID=y
CONFIG_CGROUP_NET_PRIO=y
CONFIG_LWTUNNEL_BPF=y
CONFIG_BPF_STREAM_PARSER=y
CONFIG_NET_PKTGEN=m
CONFIG_NET_DROP_MONITOR=m
CONFIG_NETCONSOLE=m
CONFIG_ETHTOOL_NETLINK=y
CONFIG_NETWORK_PHY_TIMESTAMPING=y
CONFIG_NETDEVSIM=m
CONFIG_DEBUG_NET=y
CONFIG_FAIL_SKB_REALLOC=y

#
# Beside net/core
#
CONFIG_DCB=y
CONFIG_NET_L3_MASTER_DEV=y
CONFIG_NETLABEL=y
CONFIG_NET_NSH=m
CONFIG_INET_PSP=y
CONFIG_TLS=m
CONFIG_TLS_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS=y
CONFIG_XDP_SOCKETS_DIAG=m
CONFIG_DNS_RESOLVER=m
CONFIG_NETLINK_DIAG=m
CONFIG_PACKET_DIAG=m

#
# KUnit tests
#
CONFIG_NET_TEST=m
CONFIG_NETDEV_ADDR_LIST_TEST=m
CONFIG_NET_HANDSHAKE_KUNIT_TEST=m
